==Battleground==
*3 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*2 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Gabriel]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**5 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
**2 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Because of the Gabriels and Aku Doges at the start, this stage can be hard to stall on for money. It is recommended that you bring an Area Attacker with slow movement speed that can deal with the 5 starting peons and still give you enough time to save up money. Something like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Delinquent Cat]] or [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]] can work. Once the base is hit, spawn [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] and spam meatshields (recommended to have 3-4). Again area attack units such as Paris Cat Become handy here to deal with the new wave of peons and let Bahamut or other Nukers to kill off the Aku Gories.

